{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374260-does-anyone-have-a-map-of-the-heptegram","id":1374260,"title":"Does anyone have a map of the Heptegram?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-11T17:48:41-07:00","id":1374260,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon7.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Does anyone have a map of the Heptegram?","content":"Has anyone ever made a home-brewed map of the Heptegram?<br /> <br /> I'm not aware of any official maps, but please correct me if I'm wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-12T17:29:34-07:00","id":1374458,"title":"","content":"I've got to admit I'm surprised no one has made a map of The Heptegram before, given it's popularity for Dynastic School Games &amp; such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T00:05:45-07:00","id":1374516,"title":"","content":"Ive set games in other schools of the Realm but sadly not in the Heptagram, sorry i can't help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T04:01:16-07:00","id":1374538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374260-does-anyone-have-a-map-of-the-heptegram?p=1374516#post1374516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ive set games in other schools of the Realm but sadly not in the Heptagram, sorry i can't help.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. Which schools?<br /> <br /> Did you make any maps??? I would love to see example maps for inspiration. Also, I'd just love to see them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T09:07:10-07:00","id":1374571,"title":"","content":"Yep - I second the Above <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T10:22:12-07:00","id":1374589,"title":"","content":"There's the Stephenls map of Creation (2E). Not massively helpful but: <a href=\"http://hd42.de/images/exalted/Creation_Map_v7.1c.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">http://hd42.de/images/exalted/Creation_Map_v7.1c.jpg</a><br /> <br /> There's SerAaron's 3E(ish) Blessed Isle map which is a little better: <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/seraaronart/art/The-Blessed-Isle-Highly-Detailed-2nd-Ed-Map-695948520\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/seraarona...-Map-695948520</a><br /> <br /> Maps of Hogwarts: <a href=\"https://www.hp-lexicon.org/place/atlas-wizarding-world/atlas-of-hogwarts/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.hp-lexicon.org/place/atl...s-of-hogwarts/</a><br /> <br /> Hogwarts floor plans: <a href=\"https://www.hp-lexicon.org/place/atlas-wizarding-world/atlas-of-hogwarts/hogwarts-castle-floor-floor-introduction/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.hp-lexicon.org/place/atl...-introduction/</a><br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/KvFLTsEqDzQ?t=2547\" target=\"_blank\">This video</a> has a lot of additional information.<br /> <br /> Aspect Book Fire describes the Heptagram thusly:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">I had heard that navigating the channel to the Heptagram was a difficult feat and one that had bested many kubernetes who\u2019ve made the attempt \u2014 unauthorized ones at any rate. That reputation comes almost entirely from the air and water elementals serving the school. They see that only ships that ought to make it to and from the Heptagram do so. All others are nudged toward rocks or otherwise made to founder. [...]<br /> <br /> The Heptagram must be among the most fascinating places in all of Creation. While I was there, I took it for granted, as one cannot help but take for granted those things with which one becomes familiar through daily contact. My first thought upon disembarking from the ship was how remarkable the architecture was. Contrasted to the flawless Manses of the Heptagram, Realm architecture in all but the largest cities exemplifies sloppy, second-rate geomancy. In sharp contrast, every building on that island is built to the most exacting geomantic principles known. My initial impression was something along the lines of \u201cWow. This is the real thing.\u201d In some ways, it was like looking through a window into the First Age, when every building was created by a truly skilled architect using the best materials possible, not just what happens to be convenient. The school itself comprises seven enormous buildings, each of which illustrates a specific model of Manse construction. The buildings are placed in very specific geomantic relation to each other to ensure that the flow of Essence is both plentiful and orderly. [...]</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aspect Book Earth adds:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Versino,the: A destroyed school that was an early model for the Heptagram. Built on the south-eastern tip of the Isle of Voices, it welcomed students wishing to learn demon summoning and sorcery. The school was destroyed during Mnemon\u2019s time there, and the Heptagram was built well away from the cursed ruins. [...]<br /> <br /> I [Mnemon] visit the Isle of Voices every decade or so. The Heptagram lies on the southwestern shore, and the south-eastern part of the island remains mostly untouched. [...] We rode on horses to the site of the Versino. When the school fell, it created, instead of a pile of rubble, a crater. [...]</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Aspect Book Wood elaborates/contradicts:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Insofar as the building of the campus, the Heptagram would be built to the far north of the Versino\u2019s ruin, on the same island. Above the crashing waves of the Great Inland Sea, the tower of the Heptagram would rise like a pillar of wisdom presenting itself to the rolling blue. Housing for the college\u2019s students would be situated around the tower and along the cliff \u2019s edge, always serving as a reminder of the precarious nature of the path of true knowledge.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Compass Blessed Isle states:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Along the northern shore of the Blessed Isle, under skies that often see storms blowing in from the bitter North, lies the Isle of Voices. [...] The people who work the land and sea around the island are quite knowledgeable in the folk magics common to peasantry, and even to some of the higher thaumaturgies of mortals. People who hail from the Isle of Voices are considered to be strange at best, mad at worst, for most people on the Isle of Voices have seen and experienced stranger and more arcane things than the average graduate of the Heptagram.[...]<br /> <br /> Once a school of sorcery, the Versino was nowhere near as prestigious as the Heptagram. [...] Regardless, something went terribly wrong in RY 385. [...] The ruins have collapsed in on themselves into a pitted crater, and wards of salt and sorcery hem in whatever horrible, cursed things might yet dwell there.[...]<br /> <br /> The Heptagram is one of the four Great Academies of the Scarlet Empire. At any given time, there are no more than 70 regular students here, plus upward of 10 advanced students, directly apprenticed to one of the masters of the Heptagram. The Heptagram is named for its symbol, a seven-pointed star. Each point of this star represents one of the great libraries of the academy. These libraries represent the greatest accumulation of lore in all the Realm, and those who study here know precisely how fortunate they are to have access to them. [...]<br /> <br /> There are 14 great buildings set up in a ring around a tall, central tower in the compound that makes up the Heptagram. Along the outer ring, the largest of these buildings are the Libraries of the Heptagram, and the smaller buildings between them are the dormitories. Each one of the dormitories is equipped with eating space, luxurious two-student accommodations, and personal laboratories and workspace appropriate to the library to which that dormitory is assigned. The Libraries include:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of Terrestrial Puissance:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> A student\u2019s first year </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">in the Heptagram is spent in the Hall of Terrestrial Puis</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">sance, learning the very basics of magic itself, as well as </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">theories of elemental Essence. [...]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of the Nesting Dragon:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> The library where </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">theories of mortal geomancy are taught, along with a deeper </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">understanding of demesnes and manses. [...]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of the Jade Cauldron:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Alchemy, herbalism </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">and similar endeavors are the topics at the Hall of the Jade </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Cauldron, which teaches the properties of distillation and </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">alchemical transformation.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of Ancient Lore:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> The Hall of Ancient Lore </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">teaches not only basic mortal enchantment technique, but </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">also the art of artifi</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">cing, the creation of artifacts. [...]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of the Cerulean Glyph:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> The magical theories of </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">warding and sanctification make up the bulk of this Library\u2019s </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">curriculum. [...]</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of Celestial Puissance:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> The students of the </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Hall of Celestial Puissance learn about the vagaries of the </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">Heavenly sky and those that dwell there. It is a course in </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">not only the nature of those spirits referred to as gods and </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">their culture, but also the insights into the nature of Fate so </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">often reflected in the sky, through astronomy. Other forms </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">of divination are studied here, as well, particularly Exalted </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">sorcery of revelation.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:serif\">\u2022 </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">The Hall of Verdigris:</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\"> Not all students are permitted entry </span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">into the Hall of Verdigris, the Heptagram\u2019s Library of Demon</span><span style=\"font-family:serif\">ology. [...]</span><br /> <br /> The central tower is called the Dominie\u2019s Tower, and it is a powerful (i.e., five-dot) Air-aspected manse. It contains the dominie\u2019s quarters and personal workspace, as well as the libraries of full Terrestrial sorcery. Rumor has that it also boasts vaults filled with artifacts and ancient wonders of the First Age. The bottom floor of the Dominie\u2019s Tower is the Great Hall, a huge chamber where the entire population of the school can be gathered. There is a bell atop the Dominie\u2019s Tower that remains silent save by the will of the bearer of the hearthstone of the Dominie\u2019s Tower. Should this bell be rung, it is considered imperative that every student and instructor stop what he or she is doing and go immediately to the Great Hall. Needless to say, this bell rings only in emergencies, for fear of interrupting delicate magical operations and the disasters that usually come of doing so. [...]<br /> <br /> The Heptagram is well defended, indeed. [...] Powerful spells of warding are woven into the walls of the Heptagram, spells cast not merely by the Dragon-Blooded, but by Sidereals wielding Celestial Circle Sorcery.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The White Treatise says:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">THE HEPTAGRAM<br /> <br /> The first thing a new student notices, as she sees the Realm\u2019s only sanctioned sorcerous academy, is how small it is. The entire campus covers less than acre, in a valley somewhat sheltered from the perpetual wind. None of its eight elaborately carved stone towers rise more than 150 feet. The seven outer towers hold the libraries that give the Heptagram its name, as well as laboratories. The central tower, the largest and tallest, holds the dominie\u2019s office and the school\u2019s main assembly hall. Seven broad halls built of the island\u2019s native gray granite and black basalt link the seven towers. These halls hold student dormitories, classrooms, kitchens and all the other necessary facilities. No hall is more than two stories high. The Heptagram has three layers of cellars, however, so the entire complex is larger than it appears. Some students suspect it is much larger than it appears.<br /> <br /> Next, a student notices how many areas are roped off and guarded by demons. Even the most unruly young Dynast soon learns to respect instructions where not to go; the lesson usually comes from a classmate\u2019s death. (The enchanted plague confined in a North Tower laboratory claims at least one daredevil every year.) The whole island was odd and dangerous before generations of student and faculty experiments \u2014 no surprise, since the whole island is a powerful demesne. Kaleidoscopic rains, a grove of talking brass trees and a tor that invariably draws lightning from storms are only a few of the sports found on the Isle of Voices. The island\u2019s small population of farmers and fishermen take it all in stride, and students are warned to obey them without question. A shepherd might have seen more magic and danger on the spirit-haunted isle than a young Dynast can easily imagine... which sometimes pushes a student into the Ordeal of Humility before the faculty arranges it. Most disconcerting, however, is the sheer number of demons. Although only the best advanced students study demonology in the Hall of Verdigris, all the professors know the arts of summoning and banishing. Demons far outnumber the 80-some students. Wards prevent the demons from dematerializing, so students cannot avoid the sulky slaves as they cook, clean, fetch, carry, guard and keep watch for their masters.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 3E Describes the Heptagram in The Realm on page 109-111 as part of Chanos prefecture. I'm more hestitant to copy paste large chunks of current books than I am from older, OOP stuff. But it gives a lot of information if you have access to it.<br /> <br /> ****<br /> <br /> From this, if I were mapping the Isle of Voices: I'd put the Versino on the south-eastern shore and the Heptagram on the north-western shore (atop cliffs). There should be mortal fishing communities by the shore (but away from the Versino ruins).<br /> <br /> One road should lead from a jetty on the cliffs to the Heptagram. Beyond the Heptagram should be picturesque hills and groves. The cliffs should house caves (including the Caves of Qana). There should be declivities and promotories. Somewhere there should be the Black Elder Tree.<br /> <br /> The Heptagram proper should be seven large towers (the libraries) laid out as a seven-pointed star, with each tower sitting on a precipitous crag (suggesting very rocky, broken ground with steep, sharp cliffs). The towers should have dormitories between them overlooking the cliffs but not as far &quot;out&quot; as the towers which should make up the outer-ring of the school. In the exact center of the seven-pointed star should be a central tower (the Heptagram/Dominie's Tower). The compound should be walled -- though how this looks with towers sat on crags on a cliff-top, I leave entirely to your imagination (perhaps an invisible wall of magic connecting each tower-point on the star, or perhaps a physical wall surrounding the <i>grounds </i>of the school some distance away from the towers, for example).<br /> <br /> The Heptagram itself is lacking canon details. We know there's a maximum of 80 students, twenty in the first class, all students study at the The Hall of Terrestrial Puissance before moving on, the dorms have living areas and study areas, there's a great hall on the ground floor of the main tower that can hold all 80 students and ~40+ instructors. We also know that it's two students to a dorm room. I'd put the sleeping areas on the ground floor of the dorms (two rows of five double rooms), with living areas above, then study areas above those. I'd also have The Hall of Terrestrial Puissance be the most north-westily tower so it juts right out over the sea (and The Hall of Verdigris in the opposite position, the safest, most mainland position). The libraries themselves should have somewhere to practice martial arts.<br /> <br /> As the Heptragram is situated on a cliff-face (north of the Versino if its founder and architect is taken as reliable witness), it makes sense for the southern shore to be beach (the Versino is explictly not built on a cliff). I'd put the mortal communities by the beach, but away from the Versino (so the mortals live on the south-west coast, where Mnemon <i>mistakenly </i>believes the Heptagram sits).<br /> <br /> The Versino should be marked as a crator of twisted glass on the opposite end of the island to the Heptagram (the south-east most point, the point closest to Chanos on the mainland).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":531,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","user":"JohnDoe244","date":". 03-21-2020, 12:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T11:24:27-07:00","id":1374599,"title":"","content":"In Aspect Book: Fire, Nellens Malakai's sections offer some descriptions of the Heptagram. That could be a good place to start.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T10:04:40-07:00","id":1374772,"title":"","content":"Those are excellent resources, JohnDoe244. Thank you for the links!<br /> <br /> I'll have to check out that description, KymmetheSeventh. Thank you for pointing it out. I didn't know one of the Aspect Books contained that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T18:13:31-07:00","id":1374845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KymmetheSeventh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374260-does-anyone-have-a-map-of-the-heptegram?p=1374599#post1374599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In Aspect Book: Fire, Nellens Malakai's sections offer some descriptions of the Heptagram. That could be a good place to start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically the same description is repeated in The Realm, with some variation. Seven enormous stone towers arranged in geomantic precision among the rocky crags of an island made sorcerously inaccessible to unauthorised shipping. The Aspect Book does add that the towers showcase principles of <i>manse</i> construction that put Realm architecture to shame. <br /> <br /> The Realm also hints at features of the Isle of Whispers beyond the towers - a patchwork of perils.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T14:52:13-07:00","id":1374980,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374260-does-anyone-have-a-map-of-the-heptegram?p=1374845#post1374845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Realm also hints at features of the Isle of Whispers beyond the towers - a patchwork of perils.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow. What kind of perils?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-15T17:44:23-07:00","id":1374993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374260-does-anyone-have-a-map-of-the-heptegram?p=1374980#post1374980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. What kind of perils?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was hinted that many should be dotted among the rolling hills and groves where students practice, but only a few were expressly listed: a cave where elementals kill anyone who cannot answer their riddles, a tree where anyone sleeping under its branches dreams of their death, and the demon haunted ruins of the former school of Versino on the south eastern tip of the Isle of Whispers.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T20:19:42-07:00","id":1375537,"title":"","content":"If you're into such things, Dreams of the First Age implied that the Isle of Voices was once a sort of spa/asylum for Exalts &quot;overwhelmed by the weight of their long centuries&quot; or somesuch euphemism. Bet there are all sorts of ways that might be interesting for the faculty and staff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}